A||||10||sailordude||head liner||||1||
Z||000000||sailordude||06-16-2001||06:59 PM||||Does anyone know how to repair this problem.  It is a problem with my head liner coming unattached on the cealing of my car.  It's bubbleing up on the drivers side and i want to repair it.  Any ideas? Has anyone else had this problem before?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cheever2||06-16-2001||07:27 PM||||What you really want to do is a search in the Tech section of the forum, and look up some of the websites like this one... <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/headliner.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/headliner.html</A> <P>You have to remove the board which the material attaches to, and have it recovered.  Just remember the board is VERY fragile!  Use extreme care handling it.  To get it out you have to remove the visors, 3rd brake light cover, hangar hooks, map light assembly (2 screws are under the outer light covers), the seatbelt bolts behind the headrests, 1 screw in each door jam, and unhook the trim above the doors.<P>If I were you, I would get help from someone who has done it before.  You can do it, but that makes it a lot easier your first time.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000002||Philphine||06-16-2001||10:32 PM||||was someone making a fiberglas replacement, or am i thinking of another car?||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||06-16-2001||10:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Philphine:<BR><B>was someone making a fiberglas replacement, or am i thinking of another car?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think I remember reading that somewhere on here too...<P>but, I had a interior shop recover mine last year.  The guy did a great job, and reused the backing board.  It cost me $100 and it was done very quickly.<P>Too bad I'll be cutting my headliner up soon though, for my sunroof swap.  Hopefully I can get it to come out right.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||06-16-2001||10:51 PM||||Here's what looks like the best info, from the search:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006609.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006609.html</A> <P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||5
Z||000005||AusFiero||06-17-2001||03:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Philphine:<BR><B>was someone making a fiberglas replacement, or am i thinking of another car?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I know classic industries has 80's TA plastic replacements....looked at one in a friends parts business. <P>It looked like it could be cut down fairly easily to suit the Fiero from when I measured it. <P>I think they are about $150 or less.<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||06-17-2001||06:00 PM||||The Fiero Store sells fiberglass headliner boards for somewhere north of $150 (I think).  The only problem is that they don't make one with a 3rd brake light cutout.  You have to measure and cut it yourself.  <P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000007||Songman||06-17-2001||06:07 PM||||I would try a local shop that knows what they are doing. I got my headliner done in my Aerocoupe for $60, and the visors for $10 each.. and this was factory material and brand new. I was telling my upholstery guy about the headliner kits and visors. He said send them all to Nashville and he will save you some money if you can't find anyone local. $50-$60 to have your headliner done should be plenty!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
